# === Normative block — verbatim from spec/02-architecture.md §2 (QC-07) ===
# Run bundles are large and disposable. Gate reports and the perf trend are NOT:
# spec/README.md §4 makes gates the root of trust across sessions, and PROGRESS.md's
# gate table records report paths. If they are untracked, every gate claim points at a
# file the next session cannot open. CI artifact archives are not a substitute — they expire.

build/
artifacts/**
!artifacts/gate_reports/
!artifacts/gate_reports/**
!artifacts/perf_history.jsonl
artifacts/perf_history_*.jsonl
*.chunks/
.env

# === Non-normative hygiene (local toolchain / editor / OS noise) ===
# Permitted by spec/02-architecture.md §2; additions here are typo/clarification class.

out/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeUserPresets.json
vcpkg_installed/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.sln.docstates
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# Large binary outputs (object storage per spec/12-deployment.md §4)
*.f16
*.exr
frames/
sweep.db
sweep.db-journal
